<title>JAPAN: Japan May corn imports down 6.2 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan May corn imports down 6.2 pct yr/yr -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's corn imports in May totalled 1,355,417 tonnes, down by 6.2 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows, in tonnes:</p>
<p>			   May 97	  Apr 97	  May 96</p>
<p> Total		1,355,417     1,177,982     1,445,576</p>
<p> Feed corn total    866,069	 778,629	 928,446</p>
<p> Others		 489,348	 399,353	 517,130</p>
<p>Top suppliers of feed corn (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		   832,389	 776,656	 928,446</p>
<p>Total feed corn imports during the first five months of calendar 1997 reached 4,192,525 tonnes, against 4,306,209 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432-7391</p>
</text>
